  "notes": "GAAP (modified accrual governmental funds, accrual proprietary), as FY2023. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p6). Fund balance 2,045,896 -> 4,898,325 (p6): 2,045,896 + 1,706,595 - 1,356,853 + transfers in 119,337 - transfers out 119,337 + debt proceeds 2,500,000 + insurance proceeds 2,687 (other financing, printed under other financing sources) = 4,898,325. Ending cash = governmental funds balance sheet 'Cash' 2,243,330 (p5; cash with county treasurer 23,632 and restricted cash 2,540,169 separate); beginning cash not printed. 'Taxes' kept unsplit (Statement of Activities property tax 670,291 is accrual and does not tie). 'Local' is a context label (other). 'Lease revenue and franchise fees' is a mixed line with no breakdown (Rentals, review). Business-type from the proprietary statement (p8): receipts = total operating revenues 513,170 (charges 512,577 + other 593; the Statement of Activities counts the 593 as general revenue Miscellaneous, not charges for services); total expenses 490,891 printed on the Statement of Activities (p3). Proprietary cash flows from p9. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1-2), split by Governmental/Business-type columns. Detail: the only supplementary schedule is a combined all-funds cash-basis budgetary comparison (p10, not recorded), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement (p6) and the proprietary statement (p8), as FY2023. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
